case:        TC-22 — Internal notes cannot survive into a published external document
purpose:     Checks the publish step that produces the public copy of a white paper or article: internal evidence blocks and draft metadata must be removed, and a document with a malformed internal block must be refused rather than published.
approach:    Builds two small documents in a temp folder — one well-formed with an internal block, one with an unclosed block — runs the strip script on each, and checks the public output carries no internal text or marker and that the malformed one is refused with the documented exit code.
UUT:         public-doc@3
user needs:  WUN-17
scope:       capability · method: scripted
endpoint:    none
protocol:    —
test source: —
command:     bash -c set -e; T=$(mktemp -d); printf -- '---
public_doc:
  audience: x
---
# T

Public line.

<!-- INTERNAL:BEGIN -->
secret
<!-- INTERNAL:END -->
' > "$T/d.md"; python3 .claude/skills/public-doc/scripts/strip_internal.py "$T/d.md" -o "$T/out.md" --quiet; grep -q 'Public line' "$T/out.md"; ! grep -qE 'secret|INTERNAL|public_doc' "$T/out.md"; printf -- '# T
<!-- INTERNAL:BEGIN -->
open
' > "$T/bad.md"; set +e; python3 .claude/skills/public-doc/scripts/strip_internal.py "$T/bad.md" -o "$T/o2.md" --quiet; rc=$?; set -e; [ "$rc" -eq 3 ]; echo STRIP-OK
